    <record id="channel_reviews_s1_l1" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_reviews" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">How a client writes a review</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">11</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>After a <strong>completed</strong> appointment, the client can review the practitioner who treated them from <strong>My Reviews</strong> in their portal: 1 to 5 stars, a title, a few words, and how their name is shown (first name and last initial, unless they change it).</p><p>They can add any of their own photos you've shared with them, ticking that those photos may be shown with the review.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/practice_elearning_review/static/img/portal_review_form.png" alt="The review form in the client portal" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>a client reviewing their practitioner, with one of their photos.</p></div><div class="oe-callout"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-user-check" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">Only real clients</span><p>A review needs a completed visit with that practitioner, and a client has one review per practitioner at a time.</p></div></div></div></field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_reviews_s1_l2" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_reviews" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Checking and publishing</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">12</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>Every review waits in <span class="oe-path">Practice › Reviews</span>, and whoever checks reviews gets a to-do. Set who that is in <span class="oe-path">Settings › Practice Appointments › Reviews checked by</span>.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/practice_elearning_review/static/img/review_backend.png" alt="A review waiting to be checked" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>a review to check, with the photo the client chose.</p></div><ul><li><strong>Publish</strong> puts it on the <strong>Client Reviews</strong> blog, tagged with the practitioner, with copies of the chosen photos. Comments are off on reviews.</li><li><strong>Don't Publish</strong> keeps it off the website. Add a short note if you like: the client sees it in their portal.</li></ul><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/practice_elearning_review/static/img/review_published.png" alt="A published review on the blog" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>the published review.</p></div><div class="oe-callout"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-undo" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">The client stays in charge</span><p>A client can withdraw their review at any time: the post and its photo copies come down. The original photos stay private in their records.</p></div></div></div></field>
    </record>
